### Free the clipboard buffer if transfer fails

**Severity:** `medium`

Once `GlobalLock` succeeds, the code passes `hMem` to `SetClipboardData` but ignores the return value. If the transfer fails, the clipboard does not take ownership, so this allocation remains caller-owned and is leaked. Please check the result and free `hMem` only on failure; a successful transfer must leave ownership with the system.

```suggestion
                            if (!SetClipboardData(CF_UNICODETEXT, hMem))
                            {
                                GlobalFree(hMem);
                            }
```
